   "title": "Intestinal villus (functional tissue unit)",
   "caption": "Functional tissue unit: intestinal villus. An illustration of the smallest repeating unit of this tissue and the cell types in it. Under a light microscope T cells, B cells and NK cells look alike. Surface proteins tell them apart: T cells carry CD3, with CD4 on CD4-positive and CD8 on CD8-positive T cells; B cells carry CD19 and CD20; NK cells carry CD56 and lack CD3 (Cell Ontology; HRA ASCT+B).",
